cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite, in this order: the py-ananke article in
  the Journal of Open Source Software (the preferred citation below); the Zenodo
  record of py-Galaxia-ananke itself (the DOI below stands for all versions, each
  release has one of its own), to make clear that this package was the software
  used; and Galaxia (Sharma et al. 2011, in the references below), of which
  Galaxia-ananke, the C++ code this package wraps, is a modified version.
type: software
title: "py-Galaxia-ananke: a python wrapper for a modified version of Galaxia dedicated to ananke"
abstract: >-
  Python wrapper for a modified version of Galaxia (Sharma et al. 2011), to be
  used by py-ananke.
authors:
  - family-names: Thob
    given-names: Adrien C. R.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7928-1973"
    affiliation: "University of Pennsylvania"
repository-code: "https://github.com/athob/py-Galaxia-ananke"
url: "https://py-galaxia-ananke.readthedocs.io"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
# The Zenodo DOI that stands for all versions of this software; each release
# also has a DOI of its own, which resolves from the release's Zenodo record.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.13942945
keywords:
  - Galaxia
  - py-ananke
  - synthetic survey
  - Milky Way
  - stellar populations
  - astrophysics
